STUDIES={
 'plume':{'slug':'aircraft-plume','title':'Inspect the aircraft exhaust plume','intro':'Follow a hypothetical hot-gas release from startup through dispersion. Switch between gas temperature and speed, isolate a saved time, and inspect a local cell history.','steps':[('1 · Start with the boundary','The reconstructed aircraft center section bounds a 2D external gas domain. An assumed flush slot injects hot gas for 10 seconds; dispersion continues to 15 seconds.'),('2 · Follow heat and momentum','During the pulse, the jet drives gas motion and entrains surrounding air. After shutoff, buoyancy and mixing continue to redistribute heat. These are gas temperatures; the model does not solve the aircraft or ground solid temperature.'),('3 · Compare like with like','Keep one fixed color range while moving through saved times. Click a cell to see its local history, then compare it with the domain peak. A cooling peak can coexist with heat moving elsewhere in the domain.')], 'downloads':[('center_section_with_vent.step','Section CAD · STEP'),('midnight_center_section.FCStd','Native FreeCAD'),('run_summary.json','Run checks & limits'),('cell_metrics.json','Domain histories'),('geometry.json','Geometry assumptions'),('prepare_cfd.py','Case setup source')]},
 'battery':{'slug':'battery-cooling','title':'Inspect cooling through a battery module','intro':'Explore the real finite-element temperature section alongside the full-module and coolant histories. Separate internal heat storage from heat removed by the series circuit.','steps':[('1 · Trace the thermal path','A 30-cell equivalent anisotropic block conducts through a titanium casing and two bonded interface layers into upper and lower cold plates. The second plate receives water warmed by the first.'),('2 · Distinguish the cut from the volume','The map is a Y = 0 section of the 3D FE result. Material selection reveals the battery, casing, interfaces, plates or coolant. Its triangle-average maximum differs slightly from the full-volume nodal peak plotted below.'),('3 · Read transient heat storage','At 3,600 seconds the full-module peak is 63.50°C while the outlet is 27.80°C. The coolant removes about 194.60 W of the 300 W input at that instant; heat is still accumulating. A low outlet temperature does not mean a cool battery interior.')], 'downloads':[('battery_module_all.step','Assembly CAD · STEP'),('battery_module_elmer.FCStd','Native FreeCAD'),('thermal_history.csv','Full thermal history · CSV'),('results_summary.json','Volume results & energy audit'),('simulation_assumptions.json','Inputs'),('mesh_validation.json','Mesh record'),('flux_reconstruction.json','Flux correction record'),('MODEL_NOTES.txt','Model notes')]},
 'lunar':{'slug':'lunar-tank','methods':'lunar-tank-cfd','title':'Inspect propellant through the mission windows','intro':'Choose one of 35 phases, inspect exact saved liquid fields, and compare inventory, outlet acquisition and the separately calculated ullage pressure.','steps':[('1 · Select a phase','The simulation connects short, prescribed filling, acceleration, coast, settling and withdrawal windows. CFD window time is not elapsed journey time. Choose a phase before comparing snapshots.'),('2 · Inspect liquid location','Volume fraction 0 represents gas and 1 represents liquid. Intermediate values occupy the numerically resolved interface. Speed describes the solved 2D fluid motion; it does not turn this planar model into a 3D flow prediction.'),('3 · Connect the field to the system','Liquid inventory alone cannot establish outlet acquisition. Compare the local liquid field with the outlet fraction and prescribed load. Ullage pressure comes from an independent one-way 0D helium balance, not a resolved thermal or pressurant-jet calculation.')], 'downloads':[('ledger.csv','Complete saved ledger · CSV'),('Planar_Mesh.npz','Original planar mesh · NumPy')]},
 'wake':{'slug':'midnight-wake','methods':'midnight-aerodynamics','anchor':'transient-wake','title':'Inspect the transient aircraft wake','intro':'Step through retained native-field renders at fixed 20° incidence and compare the same physical time with aerodynamic loads and fixed-loop circulation.','steps':[('1 · Hold the operating point','The public-reference, unpowered aircraft remains fixed at 20° and 100 mph. Unlike the earlier steady angle sweep, these snapshots evolve in physical time within one full-domain URANS calculation.'),('2 · Inspect one saved state','The field panel retains the original fixed-camera view. Surface colors show signed local lift traction; translucent Q surfaces show selected rotating/strain-dominated flow structures. Instantaneous streamlines are not particle tracks.'),('3 · Compare with the histories','Move the time control or click a plot. Read forces from their nearest retained record and circulation from its own saved times. The short record and contour omissions do not support a validated shedding frequency or aircraft performance claim.')], 'downloads':[('Force_History.csv','Original high-rate loads · CSV'),('Circulation_History.json','Fixed-loop circulation'),('Study_Parameters.json','Solver & operating inputs'),('Run_Manifest.json','Execution record'),('Visualization_Validation.json','Contour limits')]},
}
def explorer_path(k):return '/AISolutions/'+STUDIES[k]['slug']+'-explorer.html'
def methods_path(k):
 s=STUDIES[k];return '/AISolutions/'+s.get('methods',s['slug'])+'.html'+('#'+s['anchor'] if s.get('anchor') else '')
def cta(k):
 return f'<div class="actions"><a class="button secondary" href="{explorer_path(k)}">Explore saved results interactively →</a><a class="text-link" href="/AISolutions/simulation-explorers.html">All interactive studies →</a></div>'
def body(k,intro):
 s=STUDIES[k];assets='/assets/studies/explorers/'+k
 steps=''.join('<article><h3>'+e(t)+'</h3><p>'+e(d)+'</p></article>' for t,d in s['steps'])
 links=''.join(f'<a href="{assets}/{e(n)}" download>{e(label)} ↓</a>' for n,label in s['downloads'])
 return intro('Khani Solutions · Saved simulation results',s['title'],s['intro'])+f'''<div class="explorer-shell"><nav class="explorer-nav" aria-label="Study navigation"><a href="/AISolutions/simulation-explorers.html">All explorers</a><a href="{methods_path(k)}">Model, mesh &amp; solver</a><a href="#explorer-method">How to read this result</a><a href="#explorer-data">Data &amp; downloads</a></nav>
<section class="explorer-panel" data-explorer="{k}" data-url="{assets}/viewer.json" aria-label="Saved result inspector"><h2>Explore the saved solution</h2><p class="explorer-status" role="status" data-load>Loading numerical results…</p><noscript><p>Enable JavaScript to operate the field viewer. The methods page and downloadable data remain available.</p></noscript><div data-ui hidden><div class="explorer-controls"><label data-phase-label>Phase<select data-phase aria-label="Simulation phase"></select></label><label data-view-label>View<select data-view aria-label="Field view"></select></label><label data-quantity-label>Quantity<select data-quantity aria-label="Field quantity"></select></label><label data-part-label>Material<select data-part aria-label="Selected material"></select></label></div>
<div class="explorer-time"><button type="button" data-play aria-pressed="false">Play saved states</button><input type="range" min="0" max="1" step="1" value="0" data-time aria-label="Saved simulation time"><output class="explorer-stamp" data-stamp></output></div><div class="explorer-controls"><button type="button" data-prev>Previous state</button><button type="button" data-next>Next state</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset view</button><label data-mesh-label><span>Display grid</span><select data-mesh aria-label="Show display grid"><option value="off">Hidden</option><option value="on">Show cell edges</option></select></label></div>
<p data-phase-name class="explorer-hint"></p><div class="explorer-map"><canvas data-map width="1200" height="720" aria-label="Simulation field map; select a cell to inspect its time history"></canvas><img data-field-image hidden alt="Retained native-field wake render at the selected physical time"></div><div class="explorer-legend" data-legend><span data-low></span><span class="explorer-gradient" data-gradient></span><span data-high></span><span data-unit></span></div><p class="explorer-hint" data-field-note></p><p class="explorer-hint" data-map-help>Drag to pan, scroll or pinch to zoom. Reset view restores the full section. Click a cell for its saved-time profile; select a plotted metric to return to a domain history.</p><p class="explorer-status" data-probe role="status"></p><dl class="explorer-metrics" data-metrics></dl>
<h3>Time history</h3><div class="explorer-controls"><label>Plotted result<select data-history aria-label="Time history quantity"></select></label></div><canvas class="explorer-chart" data-chart width="1200" height="480" aria-label="Selected result versus saved simulation time"></canvas><p class="explorer-hint" data-chart-value></p><p class="explorer-hint">Click the plot to select the nearest available field snapshot. Playback advances stored states at a constant display cadence; it is not real-time motion or a new solve.</p><p class="explorer-hint" data-source-note></p></div></section>
<section id="explorer-method"><h2>Read the result, step by step</h2><div class="explorer-steps">{steps}</div><div class="explorer-links-inline"><a href="{methods_path(k)}">Full model, mesh, solver settings and interpretation →</a><a href="/AISolutions/simulations.html">Analysis &amp; modeling gallery →</a></div></section>
<section class="explorer-panel" id="explorer-data"><h2>Data, CAD &amp; traceability</h2><p>These controls inspect retained numerical results. They do not rerun the solver when you move a control. The manifest records file sizes and SHA-256 hashes. All four studies remain preliminary and unvalidated.</p><div class="explorer-downloads">{links}<a href="{assets}/viewer.json" download>Viewer data &amp; sampling record ↓</a>'''+(f'<a href="{assets}/fields.bin" download>Displayed float32 fields ↓</a>' if k!='wake' else '')+f'''<a href="{assets}/manifest.json" download>Asset manifest ↓</a><a href="/assets/studies/explorers/source.zip" download>Viewer &amp; export source ↓</a></div><p class="explorer-hint">{('The fixed-camera images retain their exact physical-time index; load and circulation data retain their own recorded timestamps.' if k=='wake' else 'Field binary layout: little-endian float32, [saved state, stored quantity, displayed cell]. Geometry, units, fixed display ranges and times are declared in viewer.json. Battery detail color range reuses the same temperature field.')}</p></section></div>'''
def catalog_body(intro):
 cards=sceye_library_card()+data_center_library_card()+''.join(f'<article><p class="eyebrow">Saved results · {e(k)}</p><h2>{e(s["title"])}</h2><p>{e(s["intro"])}</p><div class="explorer-links-inline"><a href="{explorer_path(k)}">Open explorer →</a><a href="{methods_path(k)}">Model &amp; methods →</a></div></article>' for k,s in STUDIES.items())
 return intro('Khani Solutions · Interactive simulation library','Go inside the saved results.','Inspect a time, a material or a field. Each explorer connects numerical outputs to the model, assumptions and technical evidence.')+f'''<div class="explorer-shell"><div class="explorer-catalog">{cards}<article><p class="eyebrow">Wisk work · Native saved fields</p><h2>Icepak PCB thermal explorer</h2><p>Corrected steady smartphone assembly: selectable native contour images, component maxima and vertex averages, mesh evidence, analytical cooling controls and report downloads.</p><a href="/AISolutions/battery-thermal-icepak.html#explorer">Inspect the Icepak results →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Wisk work · Open-source study</p><h2>PCB &amp; battery thermal learning stages</h2><p>Seven connected stages: heat input, PCB/enclosure coupling, thermal pad, graphite size and adhesive thickness. Existing controls and results retained.</p><a href="/AISolutions/battery-thermal.html">Start Stage 01 →</a> · <a href="/AISolutions/battery-thermal-stage-07.html">Latest comparison →</a></article><article><p class="eyebrow">Existing interactive study</p><h2>Aircraft angle sweep</h2><p>Eleven steady screening cases, 0°–20°, with signed surface loading and native streamlines. The angle controls remain unchanged. All eleven cases missed the full convergence targets.</p><a href="/AISolutions/midnight-aerodynamics.html#angle-sweep-methods">Inspect the angle sweep →</a></article></div><section class="explorer-panel"><h2>What can be made interactive?</h2><p>A spatial field viewer needs geometry, numerical values, variable definitions and saved times. A video alone cannot supply those fields reliably.</p><details><summary>Video archive: original numerical exports not located</summary><p>The six older LinkedIn demonstrations—dynamic mesh waves, nonlinear tank waves, cryogenic slosh, compressible throttle flow, particle focusing and electronics cooling—remain in the gallery. Their original case directories or numerical exports were not located in this pass, so their videos have been retained. Each can gain a result explorer once its matching geometry, fields/time histories and run metadata are recovered.</p></details><p>The public rocket assembly is a separate CAD and analysis plan; the new lunar tank study has its own solved data. Unsolved battery-vent CAD has no assigned temperature or flow field.</p><a href="/AISolutions/simulations.html">Return to the complete gallery →</a></section></div>'''
